    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21745" root="شجر" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْجَرٌ</span></b>  (S, K, TA) [and] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْجَرَةٌ</span></b>  (Mgh, Msb)
<i>A place</i> (S, Mgh, Msb, K) <i>of growth</i> (Mgh, K)
<i>of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجَر</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْجَار</span> [i. e. <i>trees,</i> or <i>shrubs</i>]: (S, Mgh,
Msb, K:) or, as some say, the former signifies
<i>many</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجَر</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  The former also signifies
<i>A place of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُشَاجَرَة</span> [i. e. <i>contending, disputing,</i> or
<i>litigating</i>]: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشَاجِرُ</span>: and, some say, it is an
inf. n. (Har p. 473.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِشْجَرٌ</span>, in two places.

